# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# Cloudflare copies everything in `public/` into the build output, so this file
# lands at the site root and is read automatically — no dashboard configuration
# needed for these rules.
#
# The split mirrors vercel.json: hashed assets can be cached forever because
# their name changes when their content does, while index.html must never be
# cached or a deploy would keep serving the old bundle to anyone who had the page
# open.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy value is not "same-origin". Google's popup sets
# COOP: same-origin itself, so a page that also says same-origin lands in a separate
# browsing context group and the browser refuses the postMessage that carries the
# credential back - which is the console line "Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy policy would
# block the window.postMessage call".
#
# same-origin-allow-popups is the value that isolates this document while still letting
# a popup keep a handle on its opener. It is the documented requirement for Google
# Identity Services, and it is the default here so nobody has to remember it: a game
# with no sign-in would work either way, and one with sign-in would break loudly.